## 8. Monetization Strategy

**Recommended MVP model: Freemium listing subscription, not commission.**

Reasoning (analogy): commission models are like being a **wedding planner who only gets paid if the couple actually marries** — you do all the work up front (hosting, matching, verification) but revenue is contingent on an off-platform outcome (the tenant actually moving in) that you can't reliably track or enforce. A landlord subscription is like **charging for a market stall** — you get paid for providing the space and audience, regardless of whether every visitor buys.

| Model | Phase | Mechanics |
|---|---|---|
| Free trial | Launch | First 1–3 listings free, 30-day visibility window |
| Landlord subscription | Phase 1 monetization | ₦X/month for unlimited active listings, or ₦X per listing per 30 days |
| Featured/boosted listings | Phase 1.5 | Optional paid boost to top of search results |
| Tenant premium (later) | Phase 2 | Early access to new listings, saved search alerts |
| Commission | Not recommended for MVP | Hard to enforce/track off-platform move-ins without payment integration |

